diff --git a/deploy/INTEGRATION_BINDING.md b/deploy/INTEGRATION_BINDING.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bb07b41
--- /dev/null
+++ b/deploy/INTEGRATION_BINDING.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Integration artifact binding
+
+The checked-in manifest binds every A+B candidate file to `SOURCE_COMMIT`
+`85ad1d7224485f3c57298e71a429eb576b8d943d` and a SHA-256. The verifier fails
+closed on missing, extra-path, symlink, source or digest mismatches. The atomic
+installer copies only manifested bytes into a new immutable version directory
+using an atomic directory rename. Units bind the exact hash directory; no
+mutable `current` symlink is used at runtime.
+
+The final Git commit cannot contain its own commit hash, and a patch cannot
+contain its own SHA-256 without changing that SHA-256. Therefore the frozen
+`integration-ab.patch` digest is written beside the patch as
+`integration-ab.patch.sha256` after commit. It is an external freeze receipt;
+the checked-in trust root is SOURCE_COMMIT plus the per-file manifest.
+
+Schema migration is a separate backup-first staging gate. Neither manifest
+verification nor installation activates systemd, nginx, a webhook, or a DB.
diff --git a/deploy/UK_DISPATCHER_ROLLOUT.md b/deploy/UK_DISPATCHER_ROLLOUT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4dc5d16
--- /dev/null
+++ b/deploy/UK_DISPATCHER_ROLLOUT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# UK dispatcher controlled rollout (candidate only)
+
+This repository does not activate production. The old Coordinator, trading
+permissions, production webhook and production database remain unchanged.
+
+## Admission and backup
+
+1. Freeze the reviewed commit and independently verify the service, config and
+   exact artifact hashes. Create the dedicated `xuanjun-dispatcher` and
+   `xj_codex_worker` identities; the worker must not belong to production,
+   Docker or trading groups. Keep the ledger `0600` and unreadable to the worker.
+2. Stop before mutation if the configured repository `HEAD` is not the approved
+   `source_commit`, config validation fails, `gh`/Codex managed authentication is
+   absent, or an old/new dispatcher ownership decision is unresolved.
+3. While holding the existing database writer's maintenance gate, make a
+   consistent backup:
+
+       python3 stage1/ledger_backup.py --backup LIVE.sqlite BACKUP.sqlite
+
+   Save the returned SHA-256 outside Git. Verify and perform a restore rehearsal
+   into a new path using `--stage-restore ... --expected-sha256 ...`. Never copy
+   an active SQLite file directly.
+
+## Canary and switch
+
+1. Install into the root-owned manifest-hash directory under
+   `/opt/xuanjun-control-releases`; render the unit with that exact immutable
+   hash path. Runtime units must not follow a mutable release symlink.
+2. Run `development_service.py --check-config`; start the unit with no ready
+   CODEX_EXEC rows and confirm a second instance fails its dispatcher lock.
+3. Verify a disposable approved task: unique worktree, transient
+   `xj-codex-*` systemd unit, bounded CPU/memory/tasks, worker UID unable to read
+   the ledger or any production DB/credential path, exact-source branch push,
+   frozen CI and independent QA evidence. This is not production acceptance.
+4. Only after Release Gate approval, quiesce the old development dispatcher,
+   reconcile all leases/checkpoints, then enable the new unit. Do not insert
+   CODEX_EXEC into the old Coordinator.
+
+## Rollback
+
+Stop the new unit, retain its ledger/worktrees/evidence, restore the previous
+version symlink, and reactivate the prior dispatcher only after proving it owns
+no overlapping live lease. If database restoration is required, stage and
+verify the saved backup first, then atomically replace the stopped database
+under the single-writer maintenance gate. Unknown effects go to WAITING_HUMAN;
+never replay a model turn, commit, push or PR creation.
